                <pb facs="0859" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-07T17:00:00-04:00">July 7, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>78. Referring to my telegram 77, July 6, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="79" xml:id="d597-f1"
                    /> Under Secretary for Foreign Affairs told me today that Bolivia has accepted
                    in principle the Argentine suggestion for bringing about immediate renewal of
                    diplomatic relations between that country and Paraguay. He expressed hope that
                    the Argentine good offices would succeed but considered the situation uncertain.
                    He supposed that a decision for or against would be reached within the next 3
                    days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
